          "text": "The pattern indexes as primitive tetragonal with \\(a \\approx 4.270\\) \u00c5 and \\(c \\approx 8.736\\) \u00c5. The systematic absence of 100, together with the observed 110 and 200 reflections, supports **P4/nmm (No. 129)**. The structure is an ordered PbFCl/CeFeSi-related 1:1:1 arrangement with \\(Z=2\\).\n\n### Primary structure CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_EuSnP\n_audit_creation_method              'Powder XRD indexing and intensity-constrained model'\n_chemical_name_common               'europium tin phosphide'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Eu1 Sn1 P1'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'EuSnP'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               2\n\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M      'P 4/n m m'\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'P 4/n m m'\n_space_group_IT_number              129\n\n_cell_length_a                      4.2700\n_cell_length_b                      4.2700\n_cell_length_c                      8.7360\n_cell_angle_alpha                   90\n_cell_angle_beta                    90\n_cell_angle_gamma                   90\n_cell_volume                        159.30\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn       6.28\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nEu  2\nSn  0\nP  -2\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nEu1  Eu  2  c  0.250000  0.250000  0.1600  1.0  1.0\nSn1  Sn  2  c  0.250000  0.250000  0.5920  1.0  1.0\nP1   P   2  a  0.750000  0.250000  0.0000  1.0  1.0\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is:\n\n| \\(2\\theta\\) observed | hkl |\n|---:|:---|\n| 10.12\u00b0 | 001 |\n| 23.17\u00b0 | 101 |\n| 29.22\u00b0 | 102 |\n| 29.56\u00b0 | 110 |\n| 30.68\u00b0 | 003 |\n| 31.32\u00b0 | 111 |\n| 36.14\u00b0 | 112 |\n| 37.35\u00b0 | 103 |\n| 42.30\u00b0 | 200 |\n| 43.13\u00b0 | 113 |\n| 43.60\u00b0 | 201 |\n| 47.38\u00b0 | 202 |\n| 48.79\u00b0 | 211 |\n| 52.24\u00b0 | 005/212 |\n| 53.15\u00b0 | 203 |\n| 56.90\u00b0 | 105 |\n| 57.69\u00b0 | 213 |\n| 61.36\u00b0 | 220 |\n\nThe lattice parameters and space group are strongly constrained by the peak positions. The two free \\(z\\) coordinates are powder-intensity estimates and should be regarded as approximately \\(z_{\\rm Eu}=0.160(10)\\) and \\(z_{\\rm Sn}=0.592(10)\\); their inversion-equivalent coordinates \\(1-z\\) describe the same structure. The listed isotropic displacement parameters are placeholders rather than refined values.",
